Time Complexity:
O(n²)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Traverse the array using index i
2. For each i, traverse the remaining elements using index j
3. Check if nums[i] + nums[j] equals the target
4. If a valid pair is found, store their indices in the result array
5. Continue until the pair is found
6. Return the result array



class Solution {
    public int[] twoSum(int[] nums, int target) {
        int result[]=new int[2];
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            for(int j=i+1;j<nums.length;j++){
                if(target==nums[i]+nums[j]){
                    result[0]=i;
                    result[1]=j;
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
        return result;  
    }
}
